# Plan & git workflow (ubuteco)

Applies to **ubuteco_api** and **ubuteco-react** when implementing `docs/plans/`.

## Before opening a PR (mandatory)

1. Open the plan doc (`docs/plans/NN-*.md`) and the repo `docs/plans/README.md`.
2. Mark completed phases with `[x]`, set header **`Status: completed`** (or `in progress` if deliberately partial).
3. Include plan doc updates in the **same feature branch / PR** as the code (preferred), so reviewers see scope = done.
4. PR title/body must name the plan (e.g. "plan 09") and link `docs/plans/...`.

Plan-only edits with **no code** may still go direct to `master` / `main` per AGENTS.md — but **never open a plan PR without updating the plan first**.

## Commits: small and focused

One logical change per commit. Split roughly as:

| Prefix | When |
|--------|------|
| `docs(...)` | Plan status, README tracking, context docs |
| `feat(...)` | New behavior / UI / API |
| `test(...)` | Specs only |
| `fix(...)` | Bugfix |
| `refactor(...)` | i18n, extract, no behavior change |

Avoid single giant commits mixing unrelated plans, drive-by refactors, or "plan + feat + refactor" together unless truly atomic.

## Branching

- One plan → one branch → one PR: `feature/<plan-slug>`.
- Do not mix unrelated plans on the same branch.

## PR checklist

- [ ] Plan doc + README status updated
- [ ] Small commit history (reviewable steps)
- [ ] Test plan in PR body
- [ ] Companion repo linked if cross-stack (API ↔ React)

Full reference: each repo's `docs/workflow-plans-and-git.md`.
